     and under every chapter the library's recorded citations of it, each
     opening on the verse. It is the research shell in its Scripture mode
     (PAGE is decided from the path, and this path contains "bible"),
     which is why it carries the shell's whole engine in bible.in03.js.
     Extends `default`; the home link and the bridge bar are gone; the
     page's own bar stays — its name (#pgname, which the router writes),
     its theme button (#thBtn, which bible.in04.js drives) and its mode
     navigation — restyled to sit under our masthead.

     WHERE THE TEXT COMES FROM. Chapter text is the ESV, fetched at read
     time through the ask-dev worker's /v1/chapter proxy — never from
     bolls.life directly, and never written into our data. Citations and
     rooms come from the library worker on R2. The complete positions
     index behind the evidence panes comes from the ask-dev worker's
     /v1/evidence, the corpus site's /api/evidence read from R2.

     This is not the Scripture Index at /scripture/, which answers "who
     cites this passage". This page answers "what does the passage say,
     and what did they say about it". The two link to each other. --}}
