<!-- DIRECTION CONTRACT
THESIS: A research library that leads from authors and questions to inspectable passages.
OWN-WORLD: Inherit Academic Monochrome, EB Garamond, Source Serif Pro, ruled stone sheets, and the shared black dark theme.
STORY: Find an author or topic, compare available evidence, follow actual connections, and open or save the source.
FIRST VIEWPORT: Clear page identity above a searchable directory; author rooms pair a compact topic rail with a reading workspace. Phones use native tabs and stacked evidence. Topic comparison has a persistent selection action.
FORM: Code-led extension of the established library; no new visual-world seed. Counts keep their units; samples disclose coverage; uncertain attributions remain separate. Scripture navigation is preserved.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster carrying its provenance
-->
